  "term": "preschool program",
  "definition": "A preschool program is an early childhood educational program that can use targeted curriculum activities to improve program quality and strengthen young children’s academic and social-emotional readiness for school. Its success may be limited when childcare settings have unstable funding or weak organizational support.",
